<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<JUCERPROJECT id="OhbVrpoi" name="Frogg3rs" projectType="guiapp" version="0.1.0"
              bundleIdentifier="io.github.daguilarc.frogg3rs" companyName="frogg3rs"
              cppLanguageStandard="20"
              useAppConfig="0" addUsingNamespaceToJuceHeader="1" jucerFormatVersion="1">
  <!--
    Android build only. macOS keeps building through app/build-launcher.sh
    and Windows through app/standalone/CMakeLists.txt: see those files' own
    header comments. This project is resaved and built by
    app/android/build-android.sh, never opened in the Projucer GUI on this
    Mac (headless CLI only). The generated project (targetFolder below,
    app/android/Builds/Android) is not committed: see app/android/.gitignore.

    Sources: app/FroggersMain.cpp plus every file in
    External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/ and
    External/Sheaf/projects/synth/runtime/HostDataPaths.cpp, the same set
    app/check_android_sources_match.py checks against, wired into
    `make -C app test`. JUCE module list: the eight modules
    External/Sheaf/projects/synth/runtime/juce_build.mk compiles for every
    other Sheaf synth app (JUCE_MODULE_SRC in that file), referenced here
    through Projucer's global module path (each MODULE below has
    useGlobalPath="1"; the ANDROIDSTUDIO exporter's own MODULEPATH entries
    are left empty for the same reason) rather than a relative path, since
    the worktree and the primary checkout sit at different depths and a
    relative path would differ between them. Projucer's defaultJuceModulePath
    global setting must point at ~/JUCE/modules for exactly this reason.

    Header search paths (below, per CONFIGURATION): app/ itself (for
    FroggersMain.cpp's own siblings and "dsp/..." includes) and Sheaf's
    include/, runtime/ and juce/ (for "synth/...", "HostDataPaths.hpp",
    "Shell.hpp" and the juce/ glue headers), the same four kinds of I path
    External/Sheaf/projects/synth/runtime/juce_build.mk passes (minus
    apps/miniapp, which nothing in this file's source list includes).

    androidPushNotifications is turned off below (task 4.4): with no custom
    activity class set, turning it off would also flip JUCE's own
    getActivityClassString() from com.rmsl.juce.JuceActivity to plain
    android.app.Activity (JUCE couples the two), breaking everything
    downstream that needs the real JUCE activity class, but
    androidActivitySubClassName below (Projucer's UI and its own C++
    variable both call this property androidCustomActivityClass, but per
    jucer_PresetIDs.h its Identifier, and therefore its actual .jucer XML
    attribute, is the old name androidActivitySubClassName, confirmed the
    same way as gradleWrapperVersion above: the wrong name resaves with no
    error and no custom activity in the generated manifest) now names
    Frogg3rsActivity (which itself extends com.rmsl.juce.JuceActivity
    directly), so getActivityClassString() returns that name regardless of
    this flag, and the coupling no longer applies. Off is what design.md's
    Lifecycle section asks for ("No POST_NOTIFICATIONS request"): the
    service runs
    without that permission and its notice appears in the task manager.

    androidAdditionalJavaFolders below carries a SECOND line, an absolute
    path into this operator's own ~/JUCE checkout (~/JUCE/modules/juce_gui_
    basics/native/javaopt/app, where com.rmsl.juce.JuceActivity.java itself
    lives). This is required, not optional: getAndroidJavaSourceSets() in
    jucer_ProjectExport_Android.h only auto-adds that folder to the Gradle
    sourceSet "if (isUsingDefaultActivityClass() || isContentSharingEnabled())",
    true until this project named a custom activity class, false now
    (confirmed empirically: compileDebugJavaWithJavac failed with "cannot
    find symbol com.rmsl.juce.JuceActivity" the first time
    androidActivitySubClassName was set, with this second line absent).
    Frogg3rsActivity.java extends that class, so its source must be
    compiled alongside it regardless.

    Unlike the C++ MODULEPATH entries above (useGlobalPath="1", resolved
    fresh on whatever machine runs Projucer from ITS OWN global module-path
    setting), androidAdditionalJavaFolders has no such per-machine
    indirection in Projucer, only a literal absolute path or one relative
    to this .jucer's own folder. An absolute path is the only way to add a
    folder that lives outside both repositories (as ~/JUCE, task 4.1, does)
    to this list, so it is exactly as machine-specific as ~/JUCE itself:
    it works on any worktree on THIS Mac (the same reasoning 4.2's own
    global-module-path choice already accepts, since ~/JUCE sits outside
    every worktree at a fixed absolute location), but not unmodified on a
    different operator's machine or in CI (task 4.11, not yet built), which
    will need its own JUCE checkout at this same path, or a resave-time
    rewrite of this one attribute, before a custom-activity build like this
    one can compile there.
  -->
  <MAINGROUP id="VgRV5IfL" name="Frogg3rs">
    <GROUP id="BcbfnoGM" name="app">
      <FILE id="ZkSBvrjn" name="FroggersMain.cpp" compile="1" resource="0" file="../FroggersMain.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="oCLrZ3aW" name="Icon.png" compile="0" resource="0" file="../Resources/Icon.png"/>
    </GROUP>
    <GROUP id="bJmTPSIA" name="Sheaf synth">
      <FILE id="Wvgfygw2" name="ButtonGrid.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/ButtonGrid.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="wMqZcUDI" name="ControllerWizard.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/ControllerWizard.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="h7yfJs1O" name="DspWavetable.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/DspWavetable.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="N43xKmTe" name="MasterClock.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/MasterClock.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="cQoXsf2o" name="MidiConfigBlocks.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/MidiConfigBlocks.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="gyrDO1xk" name="MidiConfigViewModel.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/MidiConfigViewModel.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="xwnQrS7R" name="MidiController.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/MidiController.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="PeMOkIUp" name="MidiDevicePoller.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/MidiDevicePoller.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="kDyr7OSJ" name="MidiReconcile.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/MidiReconcile.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="oRu1XXdo" name="Modules.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/Modules.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="cZuzren6" name="ParameterModulation.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/ParameterModulation.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="K4TunPFz" name="PatchPersistence.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/src/PatchPersistence.cpp"/>
      <FILE id="PDjqipVJ" name="HostDataPaths.cpp" compile="1" resource="0"
            file="../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/runtime/HostDataPaths.cpp"/>
    </GROUP>
  </MAINGROUP>
  <EXPORTFORMATS>
    <!--
      Toolchain (task 4.2's measurement, on Android Studio's bundled JBR,
      Java 25): the first candidate pair, Gradle 9.1.0 (the version
      docs.gradle.org's compatibility table names as the first to add full
      Java 25 support) with Android Gradle plugin 8.13.2 (the newest stable
      8.x release on Google's Maven index, dl.google.com's
      com/android/tools/build/gradle/maven-metadata.xml), built
      assembleDebug successfully, so it is what is written below; the
      "current" pair developer.android.com lists (Android Gradle plugin
      9.4.0 with Gradle 9.6.0) was never tried, since the first pair already
      worked. NOTE ON THE XML ATTRIBUTE NAME: this attribute is named
      androidPluginVersion in Projucer's UI and in the C++ variable that
      holds it (jucer_ProjectExport_Android.h), but the underlying
      Identifier, and therefore the .jucer attribute Projucer actually
      reads and writes, is "gradleWrapperVersion" (declared as
      `const Identifier androidPluginVersion ("gradleWrapperVersion")`,
      deliberately not through the DECLARE_ID(name) macro every
      identically-named property elsewhere in that header uses, which
      would have made the two names match). Writing `androidPluginVersion=`
      here instead resaves silently into JUCE's own default AGP (8.10.0)
      with no error, confirmed by resaving a copy with that wrong
      attribute name and reading the classpath line it wrote into
      Builds/Android/build.gradle.
    -->
    <ANDROIDSTUDIO targetFolder="Builds/Android" smallIcon="oCLrZ3aW" bigIcon="oCLrZ3aW"
                   androidMinimumSDK="29" androidTargetSDK="35"
                   microphonePermissionNeeded="1"
                   androidReadMediaAudioPermission="0" androidReadMediaImagesPermission="0"
                   androidReadMediaVideoPermission="0" androidExternalWriteNeeded="0"
                   androidActivitySubClassName="io.github.daguilarc.frogg3rs.Frogg3rsActivity"
                   androidAdditionalJavaFolders="java&#10;/Users/diegoaguilar-canabal/JUCE/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/javaopt/app"
                   androidPushNotifications="0"
                   androidManifestCustomXmlElements="&lt;manifest&gt;&lt;uses-permission android:name=&quot;android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE&quot;/&gt;&lt;uses-permission android:name=&quot;android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK&quot;/&gt;&lt;uses-permission android:name=&quot;android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MICROPHONE&quot;/&gt;&lt;uses-permission android:name=&quot;android.permission.WAKE_LOCK&quot;/&gt;&lt;application&gt;&lt;service android:name=&quot;io.github.daguilarc.frogg3rs.PlaybackService&quot; android:foregroundServiceType=&quot;mediaPlayback|microphone&quot; android:exported=&quot;false&quot;/&gt;&lt;/application&gt;&lt;/manifest&gt;"
                   gradleVersion="9.1.0" gradleWrapperVersion="8.13.2">
      <CONFIGURATIONS>
        <CONFIGURATION name="Debug" isDebug="1" optimisation="1" linkTimeOptimisation="0"
                       targetName="Frogg3rs" androidArchitectures="arm64-v8a"
                       headerPath="../../../&#10;../../../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/include&#10;../../../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/runtime&#10;../../../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/juce"/>
        <CONFIGURATION name="Release" isDebug="0" optimisation="3" linkTimeOptimisation="1"
                       targetName="Frogg3rs" androidArchitectures="arm64-v8a"
                       headerPath="../../../&#10;../../../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/include&#10;../../../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/runtime&#10;../../../../External/Sheaf/projects/synth/juce"/>
      </CONFIGURATIONS>
      <MODULEPATHS>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_audio_basics" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_audio_devices" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_core" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_data_structures" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_events" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_graphics" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_gui_basics" path=""/>
        <MODULEPATH id="juce_gui_extra" path=""/>
      </MODULEPATHS>
    </ANDROIDSTUDIO>
  </EXPORTFORMATS>
  <JUCEOPTIONS JUCE_WEB_BROWSER="0" JUCE_USE_CURL="0"/>
  <MODULES>
    <MODULE id="juce_audio_basics" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_audio_devices" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_core" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_data_structures" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_events" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_graphics" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_gui_basics" useGlobalPath="1"/>
    <MODULE id="juce_gui_extra" useGlobalPath="1"/>
  </MODULES>
</JUCERPROJECT>
